course: dictionary
lesson: 10999
title: A washerwoman in history and a story
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A washerwoman was a woman who washed other people's clothes and sheets by hand, for money. You can work this out from the clues around the word. «Toad, still dressed as a washerwoman, tells her a sad made-up story» tells you that a washerwoman is a person with a job, and that Toad is only pretending to be one.
explain: Look at the job in «Her plan: the aunt does the prisoners' washing, taking it out on Monday morning and bringing it back on Friday evening.» The washing is collected, washed and returned. That is what a washerwoman did.
explain: Ask yourself: what word would fit here? Swap in "a woman who washes clothes for money" and check that the sentence still makes sense. «When they call "Be careful, washerwoman!" Toad loses his head» still works, so your meaning is right.
fact: «Washerwoman» is a noun: one washerwoman, many washerwomen.
fact: A washerwoman washed other people's clothes by hand, for money, in the past.
fact: Before washing machines, clothes were heated in water, scrubbed on a washboard, wrung through a mangle and hung to dry.
fact: In «The Wind in the Willows», Toad escapes from prison disguised as a washerwoman.
exercise: «When they call "Be careful, washerwoman!" Toad loses his head.» What is a washerwoman? | A woman who ran a railway station | *A woman who washed other people's clothes by hand, for money | A gaoler's daughter | A ship's captain
exercise: Toad wears a dress and bonnet and pretends to be a washerwoman. What job is he pretending to do? | *Washing other people's clothes | Cooking dinner in a castle | Guarding the prisoners | A train driver
exercise: Before washing machines, how were clothes washed? | Put in a dishwasher and dried in the sun | Cleaned by a robot | *Heated in water, scrubbed on a washboard, wrung through a mangle and hung to dry | Washed in the sea and left on the beach
test: Who usually did washerwoman work for richer families in the past? | *Poorer women | Railway workers | Ship captains | Rich ladies with big houses
test: In the story, why is Toad's disguise funny? | The gaoler gives him a train ticket | Toad really is a washerwoman | *Proud Toad has to pretend to be a hard-working woman | The disguise is in a railway station
exam: Which word means a woman who washed other people's clothes by hand for money, in the past? | *Washerwoman | Gaoler | Barge-woman | Prisoner
